<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Hui Shung to tender 54,500T U.S. soy/corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Hui Shung to tender 54,500T U.S. soy/corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Hui Shung Group will tender on Thursday for a combined shipment comprising 38,500 tonnes of U.S. soybeans and 16,000 tonnes of U.S. No.2 corn, local traders said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The Hui Shung Group includes Hui Shung Agriculture and Food Corp, Eagle Food Industry and Charoen Pokphand.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>			U.S. Gulf   Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> Corn     16,000  March 5-20  March 21-April 5</p>
<p>Soybean  38,500  March 5-20  March 21-April 5</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
